# Como citar esta calculadora. O GitHub le este arquivo e oferece o botao
# "Cite this repository"; o Zenodo usa o .zenodo.json, que traz os mesmos dados.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "i3ET Calculator: Light Vehicle Cradle-to-Gate Carbon Footprint"
type: software
version: 0.9.0
date-released: 2026-09-21
authors:
  - family-names: Lima
    given-names: Paulo Sergio Pinheiro
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0002-7474-6342"
    affiliation: "Núcleo Interdisciplinar de Planejamento Energético (NIPE), Universidade Estadual de Campinas (UNICAMP)"
repository-code: "https://github.com/paulosplima-netizen/i3et-calculator"
# DOI conceito: resolve sempre para a versao mais recente. O DOI desta versao
# vai em identifiers, para quem precisa citar exatamente o codigo que usou.
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22867012
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.22867013
    description: "Version 0.9.0"
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.22867012
    description: "All versions (concept DOI)"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Mass and cradle-to-gate greenhouse gas emissions of light passenger
  vehicles, reimplementing modules M1 and M2 of the i3ET model as an
  auditable, testable program with a web interface. kg CO2e, GWP-100,
  IPCC AR6. Code under MIT; documentation under CC BY 4.0; GREET-derived
  data for non-commercial use only (see data/NOTICE.md).
keywords:
  - life cycle assessment
  - cradle to gate
  - carbon footprint
  - light vehicles
  - electric vehicles
  - GREET
  - i3ET
